  "interpretation": [
    "Runtime measurements used Messenger 580 with Hush 0.21.0 paused, distinct from the static Messenger 581 audit.",
    "Physical charge loss is whole-device net loss. It includes unrelated applications, display use, wireless ADB and diagnostics.",
    "Battery durations cover sample endpoints. CPU, lock, job and display counters cover the slightly longer checkpoint interval, including its transition.",
    "Observed fuel-gauge step size describes these samples and does not establish the hardware resolution. Few steps limit precision.",
    "A zero recorded charge change means the fuel counter did not resolve a loss in that window; it does not establish zero consumption.",
    "Per-UID mAh is rounded Android attribution. Screen allocation and retrospective changes prevent treating it as directly measured app-only energy.",
    "A zero UID CPU counter increase does not prove zero execution; per-process accounting can advance separately.",
    "Job timers can merge overlapping jobs under a shared tag. Completion counters and scheduler history were reviewed separately.",
    "Global display state varied and brightness was adaptive. The windows cannot establish that capture or a patch caused a battery-rate difference.",
    "No jobs were forced. The uploader rescheduled to a three-hour minimum and four-hour deadline, beyond these short observations.",
    "Upload execution findings concern the recorded LollipopUploadService job. Other Analytics2, native or Binder delivery routes require separate evidence.",
    "No network totals are included here. Separate network analysis excludes duplicate VPN accounting."
  ]
}
